Department Description



An exciting opportunity has arisen for a Maintenance Engineer to join our Technical Department in Delft, the Netherlands.

The Technical Department plays an important role in continuously improving the technical capabilities and performance of our fleet. Within this department, the Maintenance Engineering team develops and improves fleet-wide maintenance strategies. With our Maintenance Management System established, our focus is increasingly on using asset, maintenance and failure data to improve equipment reliability, optimise maintenance activities and support data-driven technical and lifecycle decisions.



**Your role**
-------------

As Maintenance Engineer, you will develop and continuously improve maintenance strategies for vessels and production equipment throughout the Allseas fleet. You will combine your technical knowledge, maintenance experience and analytical skills to improve equipment reliability, availability, safety and lifecycle performance.

Working closely with Vessel Management Teams, Technical Superintendents and other technical specialists, you will analyse maintenance performance and equipment failures and translate your findings into practical improvements to maintenance programmes, asset information and spare-parts strategies

Regular vessel visits are an important part of the role. During these visits, you will work with onboard teams to assess maintenance performance, equipment condition and recurring technical issues, and support the implementation of improvements.

In this role, you will:

* Develop and continuously improve maintenance strategies for vessel and production equipment;
* Optimise preventive, condition-based and risk-based maintenance based on equipment criticality, performance and failure history;
* Analyse maintenance, asset and failure data to identify trends, recurring failure modes, poorly performing equipment and improvement opportunities;
* Contribute to improving the quality of asset and maintenance data within the Maintenance Management System;
* Develop and monitor maintenance Key Performance Indicators and use these as steering information for continuous improvement;
* Provide technical maintenance support to onboard and onshore teams;
* Carry out vessel visits to assess maintenance performance, equipment condition and improvement opportunities;
* Participate in and facilitate Root Cause Analysis, FMECA and other reliability and risk assessments;
* Define equipment criticality and support the identification of critical and strategic spare parts;
* Ensure maintenance strategies comply with applicable IMO, flag-state, classification society, statutory and Allseas requirements;
* Evaluate new maintenance concepts, technologies and monitoring techniques and assess their potential application across the fleet;
* Support continuous improvement initiatives in cooperation with vessel crews, projects and other technical disciplines.



**What we expect from you**
---------------------------

* A BSc or MSc degree in Mechanical Engineering, Marine Technology, Maritime Engineering or an equivalent technical discipline;
* Approximately five years or more of relevant experience in maintenance engineering or reliability engineering, preferably within the marine, offshore sector;
* Strong knowledge of marine, mechanical, electrical or rotating equipment and the associated maintenance practices;
* Practical experience in developing, reviewing and optimising maintenance strategies;
* Knowledge of Reliability-Centred Maintenance, risk-based maintenance, FMECA and Root Cause Analysis;
* The ability to analyse maintenance and failure data and translate findings into practical technical improvements;
* Experience with Computerised Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) or Enterprise Asset Management (EAM) systems; experience with TM Master or comparable maintenance management software is an advantage;
* Experience with ERP systems such as SAP is an advantage;
* Experience with business intelligence, data visualisation or analytical tools is an advantage;
* Familiarity with classification society, flag-state and maritime regulatory requirements;
* A practical and collaborative approach, with the ability to communicate technical findings clearly and work effectively with vessel crews and onshore technical teams;
* Good command of written and spoken English;
* Willingness to travel internationally and regularly visit vessels.



**What we Offer**
-----------------

At Allseas, you’ll find the space to grow, have fun, and take pride in what you achieve together. We embrace risks to drive groundbreaking changes in the offshore energy market. You'll work in a dynamic, no-nonsense environment where collaboration is key. Supported by experienced and dedicated colleagues, you’ll have every opportunity to advance your career.

* Competitive salary and excellent pension scheme;
* Performance-based salary increases and bonuses;
* 30 vacation days per year and flexible working hours;
* Comprehensive training and development programs, study budgets, and coaching;
* A truly international work environment;
* Internal clubs, committees, parties, and (sporting) events.

Allseas is proud to have earned the ‘World-class Workplace’ label. This recognition reflects our above-benchmark employer standards, based solely on feedback from our employees. Curious about what it’s like to work at Allseas? Read the stories of our people and discover more.

Ready to take the next step? Join Allseas and shape your future with us!

